#!/bin/bash
# UCI stub that plays as a compliant engine but always chooses moves that lose
# when it is White... actually we need the engine to return a move via bestmove.
# Protocol:
# - on "uci" print id and uciok
# - on "isready" print readyok
# - on "position ..." remember the fen/moves
# - on "go ..." print a bestmove
# We want White (the engine) to blunder into a loss for Black to win.
# Simplest reliable approach: if side to move is White, play a move that hangs
# the queen or walks into mate. If side to move is Black (evaluation calls
# analyse from Black's perspective too), return a legal move.

